id: CTB-SRC0010-foundation
source: SRC-0010
section: §2
kind: requirement
text: Technology agnosticism is constitutional invariant I6: technologies and providers sit behind contracts and adapters, and the core names none. Zero unjustified hard-coding is constitutional invariant I5: business, market, provider, brand and technology facts are governed configuration, each exception is declared with a reason, and the configuration and code adapters ratchet the findings to zero in CI. Author each fact once with a canonical identity; index its relationships; reference it from consumers; regenerate derived artifacts deterministically; validate consistency at repository and runtime boundaries. The architecture constitution is a destination plus enforceable rules: every rule has an invariant (what must be true), a check (how a machine knows) and an enforcement point (where a violation is stopped).
